
Scenario: generateHTMLMainMenuTest1 | Verifies that the main menu HTML includes the page title, heading, Browse Agents link, and corresponding label.
GIVEN a WebView instance
WHEN generateHTML is called with "Main menu" and "Browse Agents"
THEN the generated HTML contains the Main Menu title and heading, the `/browse?type=agents` link, and the Browse Agents text.

Scenario: generateHTMLBrowseTest1 | Verifies that the browse page HTML includes the page title, heading, record content, and ID entry prompt.
GIVEN a WebView instance
WHEN generateHTML is called with "Browse: missions" and "Mission ID: 1"
THEN the generated HTML contains the Browse missions title and heading, Mission ID: 1, and the Enter missions ID: prompt.

Scenario: generateHTMLReadTest1 | Verifies that the read page HTML includes the page title, heading, record content, and browse link.
GIVEN a WebView instance
WHEN generateHTML is called with "Read: agents" and "Agent ID: 1"
THEN the generated HTML contains the Read agents title and heading, Agent ID: 1, and the `/browse?type=agents` link.

Scenario: generateHTMLAuditTest1 | Verifies that the audit page HTML includes the page title, heading, and audit content.
GIVEN a WebView instance
WHEN generateHTML is called with "Audit log" and "User logged in"
THEN the generated HTML contains the Audit Log title and heading and the User logged in text.

Scenario: generateHTMLDefaultTest1 | Verifies that custom page titles and content are included with a link back to the main menu.
GIVEN a WebView instance
WHEN generateHTML is called with "Custom Page" and "Custom content"
THEN the generated HTML contains the Custom Page title and heading, Custom content, and Back to Main Menu.

Scenario: generateHTMLNullTest1 | Verifies that null title and content values use the default TopSecret title and heading.
GIVEN a WebView instance
WHEN generateHTML is called with null title and null content
THEN the generated HTML contains the TopSecret title and heading.

Scenario: mainMenuViewTest1 | Verifies that the main menu includes all supplied menu options and the audit and logout links.
GIVEN a WebView instance
WHEN mainMenuView is called with Browse Agents, Browse Missions, and Review Audit Log
THEN the generated HTML contains all three menu options and the `/audit` and `/logout` links.

Scenario: mainMenuViewTest2 | Verifies that the main menu displays only the supplied regular-user option and the logout link.
GIVEN a WebView instance
WHEN mainMenuView is called with Browse Agents
THEN the generated HTML contains Browse Agents and `/logout`, but does not contain Review Audit Log.

Scenario: mainMenuViewTest3 | Verifies that an unknown menu option triggers the default menu options.
GIVEN a WebView instance
WHEN mainMenuView is called with Some unknown menu option
THEN the generated HTML contains Browse Briefs, Browse Agents, Browse Facilities, Browse Missions, and Browse Messages.

Scenario: browseViewTest1 | Verifies that the browse page includes record content, a read form, and navigation links.
GIVEN a WebView instance
WHEN browseView is called with "agents" and "Agent ID: 1"
THEN the generated HTML contains the Browse agents title and heading, Agent ID: 1, a Read a Record form, an Enter agents ID: prompt, and Back to Main Menu.

Scenario: readViewTest1 | Verifies that the read page includes record content and navigation links.
GIVEN a WebView instance
WHEN readView is called with "agents" and "Agent ID: 1"
THEN the generated HTML contains the Read agents title and heading, Agent ID: 1, Back to Browse agents, and Back to Main Menu.

Scenario: auditViewTest1 | Verifies that the audit page includes its title, content, and navigation link.
GIVEN a WebView instance
WHEN auditView is called with "User logged in"
THEN the generated HTML contains the Audit Log title and heading, User logged in, and Back to Main Menu.


